<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tonton Macoute</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1959–1986</span> · Also known as Volunteers for National Security</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tonton Macoute was a paramilitary force created by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francois-duvalier">François Duvalier</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a> in 1959, officially named the Volunteers for National Security from 1962. Answerable only to the president, its members terrorised opponents through murder, torture and extortion under both Duvalier and his son Jean-Claude. It was disbanded after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-claude-duvalier">Jean-Claude Duvalier</a>'s fall in 1986, and many of its members were attacked in reprisals.</p></div>
